@using EliteIndustries.Models
@*
    Homepage about-us preview band.

    The first content band after the hero, and the page's first light ground.
    Its whole job is to say who the company is in four sentences and hand the
    visitor to the full About page — it is a preview, not a summary, so it
    deliberately carries no figures. The counters are the next band's work and
    stating them twice would make neither read as the headline.

    THE COPY
    --------
    This is the client's own "Who We Are?" text, cut to the three sentences the
    band has room for. The full version — every sentence of it, nothing added —
    is the Overview tab of the About page, which is where "Learn more about us"
    at the bottom of this block goes. The two are the same voice on purpose: a
    visitor who follows the link should recognise what they just read, not meet
    a different company. If the client sends new copy, edit both.

    THE ENTRANCE
    ------------
    .ei-reveal, plus the --left / --right variants, and nothing else. reveal.js
    already owns scroll entrances for the whole site and unobserves each block
    the moment it lands; theme.css says in as many words that a section must
    not write a second IntersectionObserver. The stagger is the inline --d.

    THE ARTWORK
    -----------
    wwwroot/img/about-facility.svg is the client's existing illustration, reused
    as briefed. It was drawn for the ORIGINAL palette — cool blue-greys and an
    #ee6a1e orange — and has since been recoloured onto this one: the orange
    ramp to --ei-red / --ei-crimson, and the grey ramp held neutral at matching
    lightness so it does not read as a wash of the accent. The kraft browns were
    left alone, because corrugate and timber genuinely are that colour. The
    original is kept beside it as about-facility.legacy-palette.svg.

    The white panel therefore no longer separates two colour families — it is
    now just a frame, giving the illustration a hard edge to end on rather than
    fading into the --ei-shell ground. That is still worth having, so it
    stays.
*@

<section class="ei-band ei-band--shell" id="about" aria-labelledby="ei-about-title">
    <div class="ei-shell ei-about-split">

        @*  CLIENT COPY. The year and the town are not written into the prose —
            they come from CompanyProfile, which is where the client's
            "Established in the year 2010 at Bharuch, Gujarat" is recorded, so
            this paragraph and the works plate to the right of it cannot end up
            disagreeing about either. Swap the prose, keep the interpolations. *@
        <div class="ei-about-copy ei-reveal ei-reveal--left">

            <p class="ei-eyebrow">Who we are</p>

            @* The client's own claim, and the one line on the page that says
               what the company is FOR rather than what it sells. *@
            <h2 class="ei-about-title" id="ei-about-title">Export packaging is our key USP</h2>

            <p class="ei-lede ei-about-lede">
                Established in @CompanyProfile.FoundedYear at @CompanyProfile.ShortAddress,
                @CompanyProfile.Name is one of the most professional, progressive and punctual
                enterprises in the Indian packaging and material handling industry.
            </p>

            <p class="ei-about-body">
                As a manufacturer and wholesaler of export packaging material for container and
                cargo, we are determined to fulfil every urgent and large-quantity requirement
                our customers bring us — across the packaging, material handling and insulation
                domain.
            </p>

            <p class="ei-about-body">
                Manufacturing and distributing at scale lets us pass bulk discounts straight to
                the customer, so supplies can be bought in smaller quantities at the lowest
                possible price. Every order is backed by a 100% satisfaction guarantee.
            </p>

            <p class="ei-about-more">
                <a class="ei-link" asp-controller="About" asp-action="Index">
                    Learn more about us
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-arrow-right" /></svg>
                </a>
            </p>
        </div>

        @* 120ms behind the copy. Far enough to read as a sequence, close
           enough that the two are still one movement. *@
        <figure class="ei-about-figure ei-reveal ei-reveal--right" style="--d:120ms">
            <div class="ei-about-frame">
                <img class="ei-about-img"
                     src="~/img/about-facility.svg"
                     asp-append-version="true"
                     width="1200" height="900"
                     loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     alt="Isometric view of the @CompanyProfile.Name works: racked stock along the bays, palletised loads on the floor and a marked route out to the loading dock." />
            </div>

            @*  The stencilled plate.

                The mono register theme.css reserves for shipping marks and
                spec rows, used here for the one thing a plate on a works
                actually carries: where it is and when it was built. Both
                values come from CompanyProfile, so the plate cannot go stale
                against the footer.  *@
            <figcaption class="ei-about-plate">
                <span class="ei-about-plate-line">@CompanyProfile.StreetAddress</span>
                <span class="ei-about-plate-line">@CompanyProfile.ShortAddress</span>
                <span class="ei-about-plate-line ei-about-plate-est">Est. @CompanyProfile.FoundedYear</span>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>
